-- title:
--   Transfer of a blow-up chart to the local Drinfeld model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an integer $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the subgroup $H_1=\,$`levelH`$\,q\,M'\cap\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times\big)$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, and the second factor is the kernel of reduction modulo $\ell$ (using $\ell\mid M'\mid q^2M'$). Let $K$ be the intermediate field $K=\,$`laurentBaseChange`$\,L$ of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`, that is, the subfield of $L((t))$ generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb L`, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb Q$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, a domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion `coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq` (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$). Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C=\,$`chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin` for $j$ viewed in $C$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ such that (`hss`) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`: every elliptic curve in Weierstrass form over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ an $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ is said to be a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ when `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` holds: for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q^2*M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g\neq 0$, and all $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, the $q$-expansion of $\tau x$ read in $\mathbb C$ through any embedding carrying $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹` equals that of $f\mid_k$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹`.
--
--   Let $X=\,$[`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, glued from $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and the chart at $j^{-1}$, with its map `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the open immersion `ιFin` of `XFin` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a rigidity statement, whose seven clauses are summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $y'=z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition at $y'$ as `hss` imposes at $y$, there are a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring map $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\sigma\varpi$ a uniformiser, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v-fu\big)$, such that: $e$ carries germs of elements $a\in A$ to the constants $\sigma a$; every level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; such automorphisms with $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$ act trivially modulo $y'$; each such automorphism acting trivially modulo $y'$ is matched, through $e$, by an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants and acting on $X_0,X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ by a matrix $M$ with $M\equiv c\gamma$ and $c^{q+1}\equiv1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, with $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$ and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both $X_0,X_1$, and having tangent directions $(a_1\!:\!b_1)$, $(a_2\!:\!b_2)$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ have distinct contractions to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$; for a prime with tangent direction $(1\!:\!0)$ the germ of $a\in C$ lies in its contraction exactly when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; and finally $j_q$ $(=$ `jqNModC L q`$)$ lies in $C$ and, after subtracting a suitable $a_0\in A$ and killing $y'$, has image $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ for some $e_0\ge1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at all $(a,b)$ not both in the maximal ideal with $a^qb-ab^q\equiv0$.
--
--   Now fix such data: a point $z$ of $X$ with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $y'=z$ and the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`); and fix a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a ring map $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma_1\varpi$, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1-f_1u_1\big)$, subject to the hypothesis `hW₁`, which is exactly the conjunction of the seven clauses above for this data.
--
--   Let `germY`$\colon C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ be the germ map through `ιFin`, `toC` the map from $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ to its adic completion, and $\mathrm{mk}_S$ the quotient map $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\to S$. The hypothesis `hJ` fixes the ideal $J\subset C$ to be the infimum of all ideals obtained as the contraction, along the restriction to $C$ of a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $C$, of the contraction along $e_1\circ\,$`toC`$\,\circ\,$`germY` of the ideal $I=\big(\mathrm{mk}_S\sigma_1\varpi_t,\ \mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\ \mathrm{mk}_SX_1\big)$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hB` fixes $B$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by restricting scalars from the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\exists\, i\in J,\ x\varpi_t=i\}$, i.e. the affine blow-up algebra $C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $\mathcal W\subset K$ be a valuation subring with $B\subseteq\mathcal W$ (`hBW`). The remaining hypotheses are: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $\mathcal W\cap L$ is the image of $A$, that the maximal ideal of $\mathcal W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $\mathcal W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ membership in $y$ is equivalent to lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal W$, and that every element of $K$ is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h$ a unit of $\mathcal W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), that for each $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho\colon B\to\,$[`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21)$\,q\,k$ (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld relation) with kernel the elements of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal W$, compatible with $A\to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, which leave $\mathcal W$ stable, through an element $(\,$`redQ`$\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of the subgroup `hSubgroup q` (the kernel of the character $\det\cdot(\,)^{q+1}$) acting by `hAction`, with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit, in the stated sense, by some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and associated $\tau$; that an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $\mathcal W$.
--
--   Finally let $a\in C$ with $a\in J$ and $a\neq0$ in $K$.
--
--   Conclusion. Write $B_a$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by restricting scalars from the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\exists\, i\in J,\ xa=i\}$, that is the affine blow-up algebra $C[J/a]$; let $\Psi=e_1\circ\,$`toC`$\,\circ\,$`germY`$\colon C\to S$, $s=\Psi a$, let $S_s$ be the localisation of $S$ away from $s$ (named `L` in the Lean statement) with structure map $\iota\colon S\to S_s$, let $I=\big(\mathrm{mk}_S\sigma_1\varpi_t,\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1\big)$, $\mathfrak M=\big(\mathrm{mk}_S\sigma_1\varpi,\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1\big)$, and $R=S[I/s]$ the $S$-subalgebra of $S_s$ generated by $\{w\in S_s:\exists\, i\in I,\ w\,\iota s=\iota i\}$. Then there exists a ring homomorphism $\Phi\colon B_a\to S_s$ with the following five properties.
--
--   (1) For every $c\in C$ whose image in $K$ lies in $B_a$, $\Phi(c)=\iota(\Psi c)$.
--
--   (2) For every $x\in B_a$ and every $i\in J$ with $xa=i$ in $K$, one has $\Phi(x)\,\iota(s)=\iota(\Psi i)$.
--
--   (3) $s$ is a non-zero-divisor of $S$.
--
--   (4) $\Phi(b)\in R$ for every $b\in B_a$.
--
--   (5) (Fibre injectivity at the ends.) For every $b\in B_a$: if $\Phi(b)$ can be written as
--   $$\Phi(b)=\big(\iota(\mathrm{mk}_S\sigma_1\varpi_t)\cdot s^{-1}\big)\,r+\sum_{k<n}\iota(m_k)\,r'_k$$
--   for some $n$, some $r\in R$, some $m_k\in\mathfrak M$ and some $r'_k\in R$ (with $s^{-1}$ the inverse of $s$ in $S_s$), then there exist $b'\in B_a$, an integer $n$, elements $c_k\in y\subset C$ and $b''_k\in B_a$ $(k<n)$ such that, in $K$,
--   $$b=\varpi_t\,a^{-1}\,b'+\sum_{k<n}c_k\,b''_k .$$
--
--   This is the transfer step comparing the global blow-up chart $C[J/a]$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra along the weighted centre $J$ with the blow-up $S[I/s]$ of the completed Drinfeld chart at the supersingular point $y$: the map $\Phi$ realises the global chart inside the local one, and the last clause says that an element of $C[J/a]$ whose image lies in the exceptional part of the local blow-up already lies in $(\varpi_t/a)C[J/a]+yC[J/a]$. It is stated in the auxiliary $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame, with the guard prime $\ell\equiv11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ replacing a full auxiliary level, so that it applies for all primes $q$, and it feeds the construction of monic integral equations for the quotients $i/a$ on the supersingular fibre.
